# UI Design System

## Design token architecture

All design tokens flow from a single TypeScript config:

```
src/lib/design-system/tokens.ts  (edit here)
        ↓  npm run generate:theme
src/lib/design-system/generated-theme.css  (auto-generated — never edit)
        ↓  @import in globals.css
src/app/globals.css @theme inline  (registers tokens for Tailwind)
        ↓
Tailwind classes in components  (bg-primary, text-player-muted, etc.)
```

### Changing the theme

1. Edit `src/lib/design-system/tokens.ts`
2. Run `npm run generate:theme`
3. Done — every component picks up the new values

### Adding a new color token

1. Add the key to **both** `colors.light` and `colors.dark` in `tokens.ts` (the generator validates parity and will fail if one is missing)
2. Run `npm run generate:theme` to emit the CSS variable
3. Register the Tailwind alias in `globals.css` inside `@theme inline`: `--color-my-token: var(--my-token);`
4. Use `bg-my-token`, `text-my-token`, etc. in components

### Rules

- **Never** hardcode `oklch()`, `#hex`, `rgb()`, `hsl()`, `bg-zinc-*`, or `text-zinc-*` in component files.
- **Never** edit `generated-theme.css` by hand — it is overwritten by the generator.
- For JS-side color values (e.g. Razorpay `theme.color`), import from `@/lib/design-system`:

```typescript
import { tokens } from "@/lib/design-system";
// tokens.brand.primaryHex → "#1DB954"
```

### Theme identity

The app uses a **Spotify-like** dark music UI with **green** accents:

- **Base**: True-black / `#121212` surfaces (no purple tint)
- **Primary accent**: Spotify green (`#1DB954` / hue 145) for CTAs, play buttons, progress, and active states
- **Primary foreground**: Near-black text/icons on green (Spotify play-button pattern)
- **Surfaces**: Solid elevated cards (`bg-card`) over a darker page background
- **Borders**: Subtle white opacity on dark (`oklch(1 0 0 / 10%)`)
- **Radius**: `0.5rem` base — 8px cards; play controls stay `rounded-full`
- **Light mode**: White content area with black inverted chrome (navbar, sidebar, player, footer)

When adding new components, keep the music-player feel:
- Prefer solid `bg-card` over heavy glassmorphism
- Use `border-border/50` for quiet dividers
- Green is for interactive/playing states only — keep the rest neutral gray/black

### Available semantic tokens

| Token group | Tailwind classes | Purpose |
|-------------|-----------------|---------|
| Core | `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground` | Standard shadcn/ui palette |
| Player | `bg-player-bg`, `border-player-border`, `text-player-muted`, `text-player-disabled` | Bottom player chrome |
| Admin | `bg-admin-bg`, `text-admin-muted` | Admin table headers and secondary text |
| Status | `bg-success-bg`, `text-success-text` | Verified/published badges |
| Accents | `bg-gradient-accent`, `to-progress-end`, `bg-play-button` | Gradients, play button, progress bar |
| Sidebar | `bg-sidebar`, `text-sidebar-foreground`, etc. | Dashboard sidebar |

## Other design tokens

- **Spacing** — Tailwind scale. Maintain consistent spacing within sections.
- **Typography** — Geist font via `next/font`. Use Tailwind text scale consistently.
- **Radius** — `--radius` is set in `tokens.ts`. Use `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl` consistently per component type.
- **Icons** — `lucide-react` only. Keep icon sizing consistent: `h-4 w-4`, `h-5 w-5`.

## Page headings

Use the `page-title` utility class (`text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl`) for all top-level page headings. Do not hand-roll heading styles.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — uses page-title
<h1 className="page-title">My Beats</h1>

// ❌ BAD — inconsistent hand-rolled styles
<h1 className="text-xl font-bold">My Packs</h1>
<h1 className="text-lg font-semibold">My Library</h1>
<h1 className="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Studio</h1>
```

For sub-page headings (edit forms, narrow pages), use `text-2xl font-semibold`.

## Button sizing convention

Use consistent sizes by context. Never mix sizes within the same button group.

| Context | Size | Tailwind height |
|---------|------|-----------------|
| Page header actions | `sm` | `h-8` |
| Inline card actions | `sm` | `h-8` |
| Form submit buttons | `default` (omit prop) | `h-9` |
| Modal / dialog actions | `default` | `h-9` |
| Empty state primary CTA | `lg` | `h-10` |
| Icon-only buttons | `icon` | `h-9 w-9` |

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — all header buttons use size="sm"
<div className="flex gap-2">
  <Button asChild variant="outline" size="sm"><Link href="/">Home</Link></Button>
  <Button asChild variant="outline" size="sm"><Link href="/studio/beats">My Beats</Link></Button>
  <Button asChild size="sm"><Link href="/upload">Upload</Link></Button>
</div>

// ❌ BAD — mixed sizes in same group
<div className="flex gap-2">
  <Button size="sm">Home</Button>
  <Button>Upload</Button>  {/* default size — mismatched */}
</div>
```

## Cursor pointer

A global CSS rule in `globals.css` applies `cursor: pointer` to all interactive elements (`button`, `[role="button"]`, `select`, `summary`, checkbox, radio, submit, reset). Do NOT add `cursor-pointer` to individual components — the global rule handles it.

For non-standard clickable elements (e.g. clickable `<div>`, `<tr>`, cards), add `cursor-pointer` in the component's `className`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — buttons get pointer automatically via global CSS
<Button size="sm">Upload</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — clickable card needs explicit cursor-pointer
<div onClick={handleClick} className="cursor-pointer rounded-xl border p-4">

// ❌ BAD — redundant cursor-pointer on a button
<Button className="cursor-pointer" size="sm">Upload</Button>
```

## Visual hierarchy

Every page must have clear:
- **Primary focus** — one main heading, one primary CTA
- **Content density** — appropriate whitespace, not cramped or too sparse
- **Scanability** — users should understand the page in 3 seconds

## Responsive design (mobile-first)

Review every screen for: **mobile → tablet → laptop → desktop → ultra-wide**

```typescript
// ✅ Mobile-first breakpoints
className="text-sm sm:text-base lg:text-lg"
className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4"
className="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"
```

- No horizontal scrolling on any breakpoint.
- Touch targets minimum 44×44px on mobile.
- Test sticky elements don't overlap on small screens.

## Dark mode

- Every component must support light and dark mode.
- Use Tailwind `dark:` variant or CSS custom properties — never hardcoded colors.
- When adding semantic tokens, provide appropriate values in **both** `light` and `dark` in `tokens.ts`.
- Test contrast ratios in both modes.

## Empty states

Never leave blank screens. Every data-driven view needs:
- **Empty** — helpful message + CTA to add content
- **Error** — user-friendly message + retry action
- **Loading** — skeleton (preferred) or spinner
- **No results** — search/filter feedback + suggestion
- **Offline** — graceful degradation message

## Skeleton loading

Prefer skeletons over spinners. Provide `loading.tsx` for route groups.

## Animations

- Subtle transitions only (`transition-colors`, `transition-opacity`).
- No decorative animations.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — use Tailwind `motion-safe:` / `motion-reduce:`.

## Component naming

| Type | Pattern | Location |
|------|---------|----------|
| Shared | `PascalCase.tsx` | `src/components/` |
| Client wrappers | `*Client.tsx` | Colocated with page |
| Forms | `*Form.tsx` | Colocated or `src/features/` |
| UI primitives | `kebab-case.tsx` | `src/components/ui/` |
| Layout | `PascalCase.tsx` | `src/components/layout/` |
